<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 17 February, from 1600 to 1979.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1600">1600 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">426 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Giordano Bruno is burned at the stake in Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Condemned by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-inquisition">Inquisition</a> for heresy, the Dominican philosopher was burned in the Campo de' Fiori. His views included an infinite universe with countless worlds; a statue of him now stands there.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1801">1801 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">225 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">House elects Thomas Jefferson President after an electoral tie</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the 36th ballot, the House of Representatives broke the tie between Jefferson and his running mate Aaron Burr. The crisis led to the Twelfth Amendment, separating votes for President and Vice-President.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1863">1863 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">163 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Committee that became the Red Cross meets in Geneva</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Five Genevans, including Henri Dunant, founded a committee to aid wounded soldiers, inspired by Dunant's account of Solferino. It became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/international-committee-of-the-red-cross">International Committee of the Red Cross</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1864">1864 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">162 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">H. L. Hunley sinks USS Housatonic</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Confederate submarine rammed a torpedo into the Union warship off Charleston, the first sinking of an enemy ship by a submarine. The Hunley was lost with all eight crew that night.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1933">1933 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">93 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First issue of News-Week is published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The weekly news magazine, later Newsweek, was launched in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> as a rival to Time. It became one of the leading American news weeklies of the 20th century.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1979">1979 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">47 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">China invades Vietnam</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Chinese troops crossed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>'s northern border to punish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a> for invading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a>. Both sides claimed victory after a month of fighting that cost tens of thousands of lives.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a></div></div></li></ol>
